<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aleramo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 991</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Aleram</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aleramo was a nobleman in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, of Frankish descent, who in 967 was confirmed by Emperor Otto I as margrave of lands in the hills south of the Po between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a> and the Ligurian coast. He founded the Aleramici dynasty, from which descended the marquises of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a>, Saluzzo and other Piedmontese and Ligurian houses.</p></div>
